---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles information when you visit the site.`}
  lede="A plain-language summary of the information involved in visiting our site."
  updated="September 26, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This page describes how {SITE.name} handles information when you visit
    <strong>{SITE.url}</strong>. We do not currently offer accounts, a contact form or an email newsletter.
  </p>

  <h2>Information involved in a visit</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may process ordinary request information, such as your IP address,
    browser, requested page and time of visit, to deliver the site and keep it working.
    Images, fonts and other embedded resources may be requested from their providers directly.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not ask you to submit a name, email address or payment details through this site.
    If that changes, we will update this page before enabling a new form or service.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site includes support for Google AdSense. When advertising is enabled, Google and its
    partners may use cookies or similar technologies to deliver and measure ads. Our page sets
    Google Consent Mode defaults to denied; available consent controls depend on the advertising
    setup and your region. For more information and ad preferences, visit
    <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Google My Ad Center</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Articles may link to retailers and other websites. Their privacy practices apply once you
    visit them. See our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a> for information about affiliate links.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights concerning personal information held by
    service providers involved in your visit. You can manage advertising preferences through the
    link above and your browser settings. A direct address for questions and privacy requests is
    being configured; we will publish it on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> when ready.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when the site or its data practices change and revise the date above.
  </p>

  <hr />
  <p><em>This page should be reviewed against the site's actual hosting and advertising configuration before launch.</em></p>
</PageLayout>
